{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming","id":273974,"title":"Limits on Lunar size and swarming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-06T10:04:21-07:00","id":273974,"title":"Limits on Lunar size and swarming","content":"So, I hope that Lunars will be able to transform into an entire swarm of bugs, in addition to just one individual bug.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure that Lunars will be able to shapeshift into a giant bug. Bugzilla.<br /> <br /> If they can achieve those two extremes, does it not seem acceptable that a Lunar could become a swarm of man-sized bugs? Or more modestly, a small battle group of a Lunar and his Kage Bunshin clones?<br /> <br /> <br /> What are the appropriate upper limits on Lunar's giant-ness, massive swarm-ness, and Kage Bunshin-ness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:08:13-07:00","id":273996,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm not sure I'm in favor of a Lunar being able to turn into things like a swarm (of any size) or a terrain feature (as in 2e).<br /> <br /> Allowing Kage Bunshin is probably too OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:08:49-07:00","id":273999,"title":"","content":"Being able to turn into a group of things using native Lunar charms (as opposed to sorcery - wasn't there a spell that let you turn into a flock of birds and reassemble somewhere else?) opens up a can of worms I'd rather remained shut.<br /> <br /> So, by my rules, a Lunar would be able to turn into Bugzilla, or a normal sized insect, and maybe even something microscopic. But turning into a swarm of any size is right out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:20:14-07:00","id":274004,"title":"","content":"It would have to be treated like automations or undead where they don't break morale, mostly because losing health levels because half of you broke and ran off doesn't make a lot of sense. Unless your saying there's one special exalted leader of the battlegroup of un-exalted beetle clones. That being taken into account, so long as the battlegroup doesn't get too big, I think it'd be great. <br /> <br /> I especially like using the battlegroup mechanic because it implies certain rules, like if you split up and try to go to three different cities you're no longer a battlegroup and two out of three groups just dissolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:25:36-07:00","id":274009,"title":"","content":"Turning into a battle group of yourself seems like a perfectly Lunar thing to do, and I see no reason to make it incompatible with shapeshifting, except maybe DBT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:28:44-07:00","id":274014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=274009#post274009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning into a battle group of yourself seems like a perfectly Lunar thing to do, and I see no reason to make it incompatible with shapeshifting, except maybe DBT.</div> </div> </div> </div>...And that suddenly reminded me of the Gold Standard of Lunars, Sun Wukong, said to have been able to &quot;transform each of the 84,000 hairs on his body into another form, animate or inanimate, and often bite the hairs into pieces to create even more copies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hmmm. But should that be a native charm, or sorcery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:31:39-07:00","id":274016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=274014#post274014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And that suddenly reminded me of the Gold Standard of Lunars, Sun Wukong, said to have been able to &quot;transform each of the 84,000 hairs on his body into another form, animate or inanimate, and often bite the hairs into pieces to create even more copies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hmmm. But should that be a native charm, or sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's such an inherently Lunar thing based off of the Gold Standard of Lunars, then it should be a native power. And if sorcery allow allows a way to do it, it should be worse than the Lunars' native method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:34:33-07:00","id":274021,"title":"","content":"Native Charm, definitely. Sorcery should get something weirder, like detaching your reflection or summoning your own monstrous shadow, Sparrowhawk style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:42:01-07:00","id":274025,"title":"","content":"Hm. Maybe a necromancy that allows you to kill yourself, reincarnate into a new identical body, and have your corpse animate as an undead monster under your control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:50:01-07:00","id":274032,"title":"","content":"Lunar Akuma (does that rhyme?) have got that Silent Wind Charm from BWC to swarm themselves (Splintered Gale Shintai?).<br /> <br /> Anasasi (oWoD) could transform into a swarm.<br /> <br /> Vampires into flocks of bats is pretty trope.<br /> <br /> There's that &quot;body into a flock of birds&quot; spell that's already been pointed out.<br /> <br /> I've got no issue with a Lunar being their own army.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T10:56:03-07:00","id":274037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=274025#post274025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Maybe a necromancy that allows you to kill yourself, reincarnate into a new identical body, and have your corpse animate as an undead monster under your control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, that could be a cool Abyssal Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T11:58:23-07:00","id":274078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=274037#post274037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, that could be a cool Abyssal Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I know the lines can be pretty blurry, but it feels more like Necromancy than Charm, to me. The somewhat weird requirement of slaying oneself as part of it, I think, speaks more to Necromancy/Sorcery type effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T12:40:56-07:00","id":274115,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a tough call since the previewed Abyssal Charms we've seen so far really push the envelope for an Ability-based Charmset far beyond anything that Solars typically do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T19:36:33-07:00","id":274390,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'd generally allow Lunars to turn into a swarm of large animals, because a Lunar that takes the form of a swarm is embodying the sense of a swarm as being a coherent thing, and that sense is harder to preserve if it's a Lunar turning into a buffalo stampede instead. I could see it being a single elder Lunar's iconic gimmick that other Lunars have never learned to replicate, in an individual game, though, because I have a much lower bar for crazy shit in that context. (One of my ideas in that vein was a Lunar who took the form of a giant mycelium web underneath a forest, and couldn't change back without destroying the entire forest, but uses spores and mushroom configurations to communicate and control animals within the forest.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T22:05:21-07:00","id":274498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=274390#post274390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I'd generally allow Lunars to turn into a swarm of large animals, because a Lunar that takes the form of a swarm is embodying the sense of a swarm as being a coherent thing, and that sense is harder to preserve if it's a Lunar turning into a buffalo stampede instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Battle groups.<br /> <br /> If a mob can be a battle group, if an army can be a battle group, if a shambling horde of zombies can be a battle group, then a herd of buffalo can be a battle group regardless of whether that herd is a single Lunar Exalt.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar can turn into a village-blanketing swarm of hornets, he can turn into a battle group formed from nothing but his own true human form, or a smaller battle group of large beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T03:38:17-07:00","id":274592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=274498#post274498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Lunar can turn into a village-blanketing swarm of hornets, he can turn into a battle group formed from nothing but his own true human form, or a smaller battle group of large beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think that logic holds up. A swarm of vermin feels like it carries entirely different connotations from a group of fighting humans, or even of a herd or a pack.<br /> <br /> Even considering a swarm...<br /> <br /> In my mind, it's still in the mold of Lunar Charms containing shapeshifting, but not of a Lunar indiscriminately shifting into a swarm the way they would an individual animal. The image that comes most readily to me is of erupting into a set of themselves or some group animal as being... I want to say special effect accompanying certain Charms, but not in the Second Edition sense where it's an irrelevant skin to a Silver Solar Charm, more like it being a distinctly Lunar Charm in which the effect logically would be conveyed through erupting into a silver burst of animals, which then blend back into each other in a matter of seconds.<br /> <br /> The idea of extending &quot;turn into a swarm&quot; to its furthest technical extremes of turning into a set of separate creatures, and extrapolating that to the idea that you can readily turn into <i>any</i> group of separate creatures, to me that feels a lot like the sort of thing that takes the Pyrian parry Charm and says you can flood a city while parrying a firewand attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T10:34:31-07:00","id":274836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> feels a lot like the sort of thing that takes the Pyrian parry Charm and says you can flood a city while parrying a firewand attack. </div> </div> </div>With the right upgrades and enough power, why <i>couldn't</i> an Infernal do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T13:23:13-07:00","id":274955,"title":"","content":"I... think this a very cool idea that deserves to be a capstone Charm of wherever it goes. Lunars need more &quot;they can do WHAT?&quot; than they've had for two editions now, and why NOT let them be a pack of one?<br /> <br /> I mean, making an army of me is SUCH a classic Eastern thing; give it to the Lunars. Let them take &quot;shapeshifting&quot; and stretch it as far as Solars stretch &quot;swording things&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T15:22:48-07:00","id":275018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=274955#post274955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, making an army of me is SUCH a classic Eastern thing; give it to the Lunars. Let them take &quot;shapeshifting&quot; and stretch it as far as Solars stretch &quot;swording things&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that statement, wouldn't shapeshifting be one-twenty-fifth of their total capability? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T15:31:13-07:00","id":275021,"title":"","content":"I don't expect to see Lunars becoming their own battle groups even if they do have an &quot;I'm hella bees&quot; prana. Battle groups are a useful mechanical shorthand for depicting groups of combatants, but when every member of that group is just a separate body of the same entity, a lot of the mechanics are going to get confused and that particular lens becomes useless. I would expect a swarm transformation to have rules based on representing a person who has dissolved into a swarm of things, or combined it with some kind of kaiju transformation to become a giant death-swarm, rather than catch on to a system hook that really doesn't support them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T15:40:02-07:00","id":275023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars need more &quot;they can do WHAT?&quot; than they've had for two editions</div> </div> </div> </div> So... they should get something pretty obvious, disregarding mechanical problems? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, making an army of me is SUCH a classic Eastern thing; give it to the Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps, but battle groups still don't seem the best way to represent it, nor anything else that conveys them becoming a large group as something complex and intricate. Even if to me some of the image feels more like... not even a Sidereal thing, possibly a Getimian one. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let them take &quot;shapeshifting&quot; and stretch it as far as Solars stretch &quot;swording things&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even allowing for the faulty premise of &quot;other Exalt has thing in same way Solar does&quot;, how far is that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T18:43:47-07:00","id":275095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=274498#post274498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Battle groups.<br /> <br /> If a mob can be a battle group, if an army can be a battle group, if a shambling horde of zombies can be a battle group, then a herd of buffalo can be a battle group regardless of whether that herd is a single Lunar Exalt.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar can turn into a village-blanketing swarm of hornets, he can turn into a battle group formed from nothing but his own true human form, or a smaller battle group of large beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The logical path to Lunars having this power is not lost on me! I simply don't think it's a power Lunars <i>should</i> have, canonically, and since &quot;what powers should Lunars have&quot; is the core principle that defines what they get, with rationalizations being a distant second, I don't feel that extrapolating it from the abilities they do possess is prudent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T19:25:34-07:00","id":275113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275023#post275023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So... they should get something pretty obvious, disregarding mechanical problems? Perhaps, but battle groups still don't seem the best way to represent it, nor anything else that conveys them becoming a large group as something complex and intricate. Even if to me some of the image feels more like... not even a Sidereal thing, possibly a Getimian one. Even allowing for the faulty premise of &quot;other Exalt has thing in same way Solar does&quot;, how far is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be obvious, but it's also something that *feels* really powerful. There's no inherent merit to eschewing the low-hanging fruit for being &quot;obvious&quot; - meeting expectations is just as important as including things that go beyond them in terms of making something be awesome and fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the Solar jab was at &quot;I sword so hard, I don't need to be in sword range. Or using a sword.&quot; In fact, let's NOT go that far, let's just finish giving them everything that DOES belong in their signature schtick.<br /> <br /> <br /> (and because I'm still chugging along through DBZ... turning into multiple selves at once is done by no less than *three* different &quot;PCs&quot; there... it should be somewhere in Exalted)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T19:57:44-07:00","id":275158,"title":"","content":"At least two different &quot;PCs&quot; in DBZ also <i>casually blew up the moon in one action, </i>for basically no reason other than &quot;stop that big monkey,&quot; one of whom was considered to be of &quot;so low I can't even meaningfully contribute&quot; power level by the time DBZ rolls around. I don't think the two settings should have perfect transparency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-07-2014, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T21:41:07-07:00","id":275209,"title":"","content":"Due to mechanical overlap with Kaiju powers like Emperor Ox Expansion. I'd be fine if things like swarming was cut from the lunar kit in favor of both a diverse and sufficiently potent charm distribution. I'm really just hoping the Lunars won't be as far away from the Solars+variants, Sidereals, and (from what's been hinted at) a sizable chunk of the Exigents this time around and that they can be easily enjoyed without feeling overshadowed in mixed celestial play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T00:26:46-07:00","id":275239,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've liked the idea of Lunars being able to turn into a group of creatures since reading about a few of the Soletaken doing the same in the Malazan books series, and I'm hoping there will be some support for that kind of character in EX3. Failing that I'm sure an Exigent whose abilities completely focus around turning into a specific group of one kind of creature wont be too difficult to come up with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/624-bejazeus","name":"Bejazeus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T01:19:25-07:00","id":275248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275158#post275158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least two different &quot;PCs&quot; in DBZ also <i>casually blew up the moon in one action, </i>for basically no reason other than &quot;stop that big monkey,&quot; one of whom was considered to be of &quot;so low I can't even meaningfully contribute&quot; power level by the time DBZ rolls around. I don't think the two settings should have perfect transparency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you entirely certain? I could swear there was a Solar Hero Style expansion charm that let you take an action and blow Luna out of the sky...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T05:59:37-07:00","id":275415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275248#post275248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you entirely certain? I could swear there was a Solar Hero Style expansion charm that let you take an action and blow Luna out of the sky...</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use Horizon-Hurling Tactic or Sky-Breaker Throw to chuck things at the moon, but without knowing how many wounds the Silver Chariot can take I couldn't guess if that would be enough to actually bring it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T06:14:31-07:00","id":275424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275113#post275113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">turning into multiple selves at once is done by no less than *three* different &quot;PCs&quot; there... it should be somewhere in Exalted)</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, Getimians. Possibly even a Martial Art.<br /> <br /> I mean, Hell, I've noted before that new Exalted means that Lunars no longer need to be the dumping grounds for all homeless powers and concepts, I might as well start pushing that.<br /> <br /> Indeed, this even carries through to the whole Sun Wukong thing (I feel that it's difficult to use the Monkey King as a reference point for Lunars, because so many of his own powers are a matter of his Taoist instruction and alchemical transformation rather than his own body... which is itself more weird magic stuff than animalistic person, considering that he was born from a stone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T15:02:16-07:00","id":275790,"title":"","content":"I just pray to Luna that they will have implented a decent system for size scaling. Leviathan - <i>The Leviathan</i> - being no bigger than a blue whale in his Emperor Ox Form made me feel seriously gypped. Especially when we had everything from two hundred feet (60m) Snow Wyrms to four hundred feet (120m) Storm Serpents to quarter-mile (402.25m) machine-gods to mile-long (1,609+m) Juggernauts in the setting...<br /> <br /> Sigh.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T15:39:46-07:00","id":275819,"title":"","content":"It be pretty cool to play as a Di'vers from Malazan. I don't remember what happened to them if a couple pieces were killed while transformed though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1970-yeangst","name":"yeangst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T15:52:32-07:00","id":275831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275819#post275819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It be pretty cool to play as a Di'vers from Malazan. I don't remember what happened to them if a couple pieces were killed while transformed though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They forgot memories or something, IIRC. Kind of like Ananasi in crawlerling form in WoD. That said, D'ivers were never explained that well as to how they actually worked. Lunars are definitely like Soletaken though.<br /> <br /> I think Lunars should probably be able to have Crawlerling Swarm Mode, but there's no point using the battle group mechanics if said mechanics aren't modeling the desired effect: battle groups are mechanical shortcuts to model a specific thing, and if you remove elements that need specific modeling (like the idea that soldiers will break and flee as their fellows are killed, or that a peasant levy will be less effective at fighting en masse than a regiment of drilled professional soldiers) then you're probably better off not using those mechanics if using them means leaving a lot of their system hooks (i.e. the whole purpose for using that subsystem) empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T22:53:53-07:00","id":276102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275424#post275424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, Hell, I've noted before that new Exalted means that Lunars no longer need to be the dumping grounds for all homeless powers and concepts, I might as well start pushing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pushing WHAT? Start taking stuff away from Lunars, and what are we really left with?<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are going to be the Host most changed from previous editions, to the point where we have a better idea how the Getimians and Liminals will work... and those Hosts are brand new!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T23:20:43-07:00","id":276111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276102#post276102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pushing WHAT? Start taking stuff away from Lunars, and what are we really left with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, remember when Lunars had gravity manipulation powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T23:21:50-07:00","id":276112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275790#post275790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Leviathan - <i>The Leviathan</i> - being no bigger than a blue whale in his Emperor Ox Form made me feel seriously gypped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, poor Leviathan only getting to be as big as the biggest thing that has ever lived.<br /> <br /> Wait...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T00:49:02-07:00","id":276120,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would say it would depend entirely on the swarm rules.<br /> <br /> If they're shit-ass like the last few editions of D&amp;D/Pathfinder, than hell goddamn no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T04:18:45-07:00","id":276165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276112#post276112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, poor Leviathan only getting to be as big as the biggest thing that has ever lived.<br /> <br /> Wait...</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest creature in the real world. A mundane creature. In a world where there are literal <i>flying whales</i> bigger than them, or elk whales out-massing them several times over, or freaking redwood mantises walking about... And this guy is not just any Lunar, he is an elder, one of <i>the Elders</i> in fact, and the only one canonically possessing the iconic &quot;Fuck You I'm A Kaiju&quot; knack. He is effectively Magnitude 7 in mass combat, when the Juggernaut - the freaking <i>Juggernaut</i> - is Magnitude 9.<br /> <br /> No. I'll just chalk it up to more &quot;Lunars don't get to be awesome&quot;, with a touch of &quot;Unless they are player characters&quot; for the sake of argument.<br /> <br /> Head-Canon: Leviathan's blue whale-sized self is just his Spirit Form, augmented by the [Mountainous Spirit Expression] knacks. When he goes into battle, he swells into an island-sized behemoth nearly ten times that size, big enough to swallow a small fleet of ships with a single gulp. At least, that was the case during the Balorian Crusade. Nearly eight hundred years later, who knows if the Admiral of the West has not yet begun to approach the mythic God-Beast Transcendence displayed by his predecessor Jormungandr, the Great Serpent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T05:36:03-07:00","id":276215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276165#post276165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The biggest creature in the real world. A mundane creature. In a world where there are literal <i>flying whales</i> bigger than them, or elk whales out-massing them several times over, or freaking redwood mantises walking about...</div> </div> </div> </div>I love weird fantasy stuff, but the point where it starts generating contempt for impressive real life stuff is the point where a few steps back need to be taken.<br /> <br /> Although I'm a bit dubious on the size for those flying whales...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is effectively Magnitude 7 in mass combat, when the Juggernaut - the freaking <i>Juggernaut</i> - is Magnitude 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, is that something he was actually given mechanically?<br /> <br /> I mean, disregarding how stupid the whole &quot;single giant monster is a high Magnitude unit&quot; thing was.<br /> <br /> No. I'll just chalk it up to more &quot;Lunars don't get to be awesome&quot;, with a touch of &quot;Unless they are player characters&quot; for the sake of argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Head-Canon: Leviathan's blue whale-sized self is just his Spirit Form, augmented by the [Mountainous Spirit Expression] knacks. When he goes into battle, he swells into an island-sized behemoth nearly ten times that size, big enough to swallow a small fleet of ships with a single gulp.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems the same kind of ridiculous overscaling that led to Solars being able to destroy entire armies by throwing somebody who would explode at them.<br /> <br /> The Exalted don't really fit the narrative space of Big Dumb Object. It doesn't strike me as necessary when Leviathan can be &quot;just&quot; large enough to tear out the hull of ships as he zooms with impossible speed and terrifying fury between them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:12:36-07:00","id":276293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276215#post276215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love weird fantasy stuff, but the point where it starts generating contempt for impressive real life stuff is the point where a few steps back need to be take<br /> The Exalted don't really fit the narrative space of Big Dumb Object. It doesn't strike me as necessary when Leviathan can be just large enough to tear out the hull of ships as he zooms with impossible speed and terrifying fury between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree. A hundred foot long torpedo of muscle, bone and essence fuelled rage is fucking terrifying. Not that exalted shouldn't have the occasional mountain sized beast, but a big dumb monster Leviathan is not. He's intelligent, experienced, leads a fanatical nation-cult and he's got lunar charms to enhance himself. He can sit hundreds of feet below the surface, target a ship with that lunar enhanced aim charm and lunar enhanced perception, then attack by driving towards the surface and leaping out of the water through a ship. <br /> <br /> Maybe he's a large blue whale, like 120-150 feet, but he doesn't need to be 1000 feet long to destroy entire navies, nor should he be able to casually munch down Skullstone's fleet or the Water fleet or whatever. That's not even counting that you need water aspected DBs or Solars to even be able to effectively fight a submarine animal using traditional naval weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:33:50-07:00","id":276313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276215#post276215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>You do have a point about contempt for things that are awesome in real life. Does not change the fact that the setting is filled with big monsters, and I have always been under the impression that the Leviathan is one of them.<br /> <br /> Flying whales are from CoCD:Wyld, described as 200 feet long, so twice the length of a blue whale.<br /> <br /> Emperor Ox Form gives you a Magnitude of Essence in mass combat; I don't really care for it, as you say Numbers=!Size, but as a reference point it works well enough.<br /> <br /> And while I disagree with Solars being able to kill an army by throwing someone at them Orbital Bombardment Style, I feel it is entirely within the scope of the setting to have an iconic Essence 7 Solar be able to cut through half a dozen small wooden ships with a single strike from his Mountain-Cleaving Blade. Now, either of them - Leviathan or Invincible Sword Princess the Elder - trying that with a First Age Ship or one captain by an Exalt, should find things quite a bit more troublesome. But that's a different thing.<br /> <br /> I guess it's a matter of preference. I do want the Admiral to be an awesome tactician, to live up to his background and title - but I also want him to be the Epic Monster of the Deep, the one all others are compared to and found wanting against.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276293#post276293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a different picture of how the Leviathan fights - it's a good picture, but it's different from the one I have.<br /> <br /> You do have a good point about needing other Exalts - specifically Water Aspects - to adequately fight him though. That, or First Age navies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:09:34-07:00","id":276372,"title":"","content":"Point of order: Leviathan is an <i>orca</i> whale, who can be the <i>size</i> of a blue whale.<br /> <br /> Also, pitting a mile-long sea serpent or whatever against Leviathan in his big whale form, I'd bet on Leviathan, full-stop.<br /> <br /> He doesn't have to be the biggest to be the most fearsome - the fact that he's as cunning as a man, as ruthless as a killer whale, and stronger than either would make him terrifying if he was the size of a water-flea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-09-2014, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:17:41-07:00","id":276381,"title":"","content":"See that's all great. Now why can't we see more of Leviathan righteously wrecking the shit of Lintha pirates and Terrestrial would-be conquistadores, and less about him sulking over his love triangle between the hilariously glurge-tastic Queen Amyana and her serial-rapist husband.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:28:06-07:00","id":276388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276313#post276313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess it's a matter of preference. I do want the Admiral to be an awesome tactician, to live up to his background and title - but I also want him to be the Epic Monster of the Deep, the one all others are compared to and found wanting against.</div> </div> </div> </div>He can do that without being bigger than they are, just like how the Solars can defeat the Primordials who are vastly more powerful than them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:41:48-07:00","id":276401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276388#post276388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He can do that without being bigger than they are, just like how the Solars can defeat the Primordials who are vastly more powerful than them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't even go that far, the primordials were defeated because exalted punch above their weight class. I don't think that's something leviathan would have to do unless he was fighting some of the really intense shit in the ocean. Most of the big sea monsters vs leviathan would probably be like watching an F-22 fight a trireme. One is technically much larger, but there's no way it can win.<br /> <br /> Also really small nitpick and I don't always point it out, but the exalted defeated the primordials. Everyone, including me, often says the Solars defeated the primordials, but it's a bad habit I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T09:16:04-07:00","id":276418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276111#post276111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, remember when Lunars had gravity manipulation powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, remember when Lunars had shapeshifting powers?<br /> <br /> By all means, let's get rid of the extraneous crap that doesn't really make sense with &quot;zoanthropic shapeshifting demigod&quot;. But when people start arguing that a Lunar can't become a pack of wolves despite the power to become a swarm of bees, I'm going to get pissy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turning into animals&quot; is what they do, and there's really not very far to GO with that idea. Cutting out &quot;become multiple animals at once&quot; seems unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T10:14:36-07:00","id":276450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276418#post276418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, remember when Lunars had shapeshifting powers?<br /> <br /> By all means, let's get rid of the extraneous crap that doesn't really make sense with &quot;zoanthropic shapeshifting demigod&quot;. But when people start arguing that a Lunar can't become a pack of wolves despite the power to become a swarm of bees, I'm going to get pissy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turning into animals&quot; is what they do, and there's really not very far to GO with that idea. Cutting out &quot;become multiple animals at once&quot; seems unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What would this turning into a pack of wolves entail? Are those wolves benefiting from all the Lunars self-enhancement magic? Do they all have a wolf's health track? Does killing one kill the Lunar?<br /> <br /> If each of those wolves is a copy of the Lunar in wolf form with all associated abilities then this leads don the path of madness. If all but one wolf if just a meatpuppet the Lunar happened to have made from their body then it is not mechanically different from letting the Lunar call up/bond/familiarize a pack of wolves. Heck, if battle groups work anything like 2E where they get bonuses based on size, this is a one charm/knack supermode or some flat/boring bonuses.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turning into animals&quot; is a <i>thing</i> they can do, it is not what they do. There are socialite lunars who might occasionally turn into a cat when they need to run away or mystic lunars who are too busy with their astral projection or summoning demons to ever bother getting a new form. Heck, there are even warrior lunars who are too busy hitting you with evocations to want to change into animals.<br /> <br /> Edit: I know you like Lunars and that they have consistently gotten the short stick. That doesn't mean they need to burrow into one mechanic and inflate it beyond hat it was designed to do. They shouldn't need to, and if the devs do as good a job as we hope they wont have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 10-09-2014, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T10:23:14-07:00","id":276453,"title":"","content":"Shamanistic astral projection should be all up in this lunar business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T10:31:24-07:00","id":276458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276450#post276450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really that big of a deal. If it's something like Host of Spirits, where each is slightly weaker than the original, and all share the same mote pool - you want them all to use some basic Charms, like Claws of the Silver Moon? You'll have to pay for it for each of them. Which means ye old staple, Excellencies, won't really be and option, which means that the opponents will simply beat them with skill.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T12:48:13-07:00","id":276585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276418#post276418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By all means, let's get rid of the extraneous crap that doesn't really make sense with &quot;zoanthropic shapeshifting demigod&quot;. But when people start arguing that a Lunar can't become a pack of wolves despite the power to become a swarm of bees, I'm going to get pissy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of it is that we can rationalize a swarm of bees acting like one entity (even though it's clearly not just one entity), but logic doesn't extrapolate that into &quot;swarm of wolves&quot; very well.<br /> <br /> Hell, I'm more cool with the &quot;turn into a weird meta-terrain feature&quot; thing than trying to shoehorn Swarm of Yeddim Prana into the system as a Thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T15:10:26-07:00","id":276686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276458#post276458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really that big of a deal. If it's something like Host of Spirits, where each is slightly weaker than the original, and all share the same mote pool - you want them all to use some basic Charms, like Claws of the Silver Moon? You'll have to pay for it for each of them. Which means ye old staple, Excellencies, won't really be and option, which means that the opponents will simply beat them with skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind what the devs have said about the rarity of multiple attacks in the new system and the necessity of using battle groups to represent large gangs of opponents, it seems like representing a Lunar-as-wolf-pack and having each wolf as a separate entity (even a weaker one, even sharing the mote pool) would be an <i>overwhelming</i> advantage. It's a big deal.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beat[ing] them with skill&quot; isn't necessary if you force the opponent to have to defend against some 40-some-odd attacks for every one they get to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-09-2014, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T15:52:02-07:00","id":276734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276418#post276418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By all means, let's get rid of the extraneous crap that doesn't really make sense with &quot;zoanthropic shapeshifting demigod&quot;. But when people start arguing that a Lunar can't become a pack of wolves despite the power to become a swarm of bees, I'm going to get pissy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turning into animals&quot; is what they do, and there's really not very far to GO with that idea. Cutting out &quot;become multiple animals at once&quot; seems unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be better for Lunars to not be able to turn into a swarm of bees than for Lunars to turn into a swarm of bees and a pack of wolves, IMO, and the fact that you feel this way is a strong argument for taking <i>any</i> swarm-form ability from them. That said, I think the current setup -- where they can become a swarm of bees but not a pack of wolves -- is probably fine.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want Lunars to <i>canonically</i> be able to turn into mycelium, either, despite the character concept I mentioned earlier. It warps what Lunars actually are if they go too far in that direction. &quot;Turns into different types of creature&quot; is not the wellspring of all Lunar thematics, so you can't just blindly extrapolate from that or you end up with things like that guy who thinks the Great Contagion is horning in on Lunars' turf.<br /> <br /> Lunars do a hell of a lot of things besides turning into animals, just like Solars do a hell of a lot of things besides glowing and leadership and Green Lantern shenanigans. Trying to buff them up by expanding the breadth of &quot;turning into animals&quot; is likely to get silly fast. Like, Hungry All-Consuming Cloud is already pushing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:00:29-07:00","id":276743,"title":"","content":"On a theme level, I'm feel like I'm cool with Lunars turning into a swarm of whatevers (whatever their size) if and only if it isn't overpowered (more powerful than is actually fun or makes sense for the world) and much more crucially, it feels like something out of pulp fantasy fiction by a protagonist who is not any kind of transhumey wotsit (which it can - Granny Weatherwax does it ffs) as an interlude between or instrument of all too human politicking and melodrama.<br /> <br /> With swarms, I feel like there's this thing where it can become... sci fi like something out of a Bruce Sterling's the Swarm or you're Kerrigan Queen of Blades or whatever where there's some science horror \u201cLike, oh my god, we're confronting serious existential stuff that challenges mankind's place in the universe or the ability of the human mind to understand reality in its true form here\u201c... Lunars at their default are not about any sort of body horror thing or losing humanity or becoming a thing in human form or eschewing the limits of a mere human soul, I feel.<br /> <br /> (yeah, I know chimeras - I think they should only be a fraction of the Wyld twisted Exalted, of all splats).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:00:31-07:00","id":276744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276686#post276686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping in mind what the devs have said about the rarity of multiple attacks in the new system and the necessity of using battle groups to represent large gangs of opponents, it seems like representing a Lunar-as-wolf-pack and having each wolf as a separate entity (even a weaker one, even sharing the mote pool) would be an <i>overwhelming</i> advantage. It's a big deal.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beat[ing] them with skill&quot; isn't necessary if you force the opponent to have to defend against some 40-some-odd attacks for every one they get to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. Should the devs go for this direction of single-Lunar-as-wolf-pack,* I'd be interested in seeing the implementation. From Vance's comment, one possibility might take its cues from battle groups in some respects, deviating where it makes sense.<br /> <br /> * I don't know that I expect to see it, but hey! I don't have a great handle on powers I expect EX3 Lunars to throw around.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hmm... I'm curious. I don't expect answers on these from the EX3 Team, but they're things I may look up when the Core is in my hands. If they're statted up in there, do wolves get any special options/tricks/benefits for operating as a pack? If so, do these come up when wolves are part of a battle group (on top of anything normal battle groups get) or only for wolves as individual actors working together? I guess an underlying question concerns how static a battle group must be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Extra question. 10-09-2014, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:47:50-07:00","id":276800,"title":"","content":"There's some kind of ground where Lunars, if Vance's past ambitions are realized, will get Medusa snake hair. That's sort of like turning into a pack, but Lunar source myth seems to like multi-headed beast monsters more than one in several bodies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276743#post276743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (yeah, I know chimeras - I think they should only be a fraction of the Wyld twisted Exalted, of all splats).</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't EX3 doing away with the Wyld-buttered clones of The Thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:49:13-07:00","id":276805,"title":"","content":"adamant siaka why are you now Dark Revlid","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:50:09-07:00","id":276807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276805#post276805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">adamant siaka why are you now Dark Revlid</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget, did Revlid use that tyrannosaur avatar before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:53:11-07:00","id":276812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276807#post276807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I forget, did Revlid use that tyrannosaur avatar before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaah so that's what it is.<br /> <br /> I think my monitor is using too high a contrast. Your avatar's colors blend together into a shape that was more reminiscent of a brown hooded figure, much similar to Revlid's green hooded figure avatar.<br /> <br /> Sorry about this disturbance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T17:45:07-07:00","id":276856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276744#post276744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Hmm... I'm curious. I don't expect answers on these from the EX3 Team, but they're things I may look up when the Core is in my hands. If they're statted up in there, do wolves get any special options/tricks/benefits for operating as a pack? If so, do these come up when wolves are part of a battle group (on top of anything normal battle groups get) or only for wolves as individual actors working together? I guess an underlying question concerns how static a battle group must be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would wager the point of a battle group is to easily represent a larger number of combatants than is feasible to run as individuals, combining that with notions of how groups of people fight together and react to fighting together.<br /> <br /> If an ST runs a mob of 20 angry peasants as a battle group, simply being a battle group shouldn't necessarily provide those 20 peasants or the Exalted they're fighting a super huge advantage or disadvantage over fighting 20 peasants as individuals. The point is to make it OOC easier to run such a combat (and end it in ways other than killing every discrete living thing inside the battle group) by having only one &quot;unit&quot; to interact with (as opposed to 20), with its own internal rules like &quot;for every X damage taken, suffer Y stat degradation and Z morale effect.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would imagine that a battle group possesses the normal &quot;special&quot; powers of its constituent entities, plus specific group-only stats like Drill, Morale, and Might to represent certain group functions. A pack of wolves would likely have a higher Drill than a random peasant mob simply because a wolf pack is a family that lives and hunts together, versus a bunch of angry people who grab pitchforks and coalesce into a mob for safety and intimidation purposes.<br /> <br /> Think about how swarms are often represented in RPG video games like Final Fantasy: when you fight a swarm of hell-wasps it's visually a blob of things but mechanically it's got one health pool and you target the swarm as a whole rather than individual wasps. I would say that is the model to reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276686#post276686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping in mind what the devs have said about the rarity of multiple attacks in the new system</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC that's mainly a response to the ol' 0m Grand Goremaul flurry and killing that notion so that making multiple attacks isn't easy and moteless. I'm sure combat Charms will provide ample ways to make multiple attacks at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-09-2014, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T18:23:32-07:00","id":276883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276744#post276744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Hmm... I'm curious. I don't expect answers on these from the EX3 Team, but they're things I may look up when the Core is in my hands. If they're statted up in there, do wolves get any special options/tricks/benefits for operating as a pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would they be proper wolves without them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so, do these come up when wolves are part of a battle group (on top of anything normal battle groups get) or only for wolves as individual actors working together? I guess an underlying question concerns how static a battle group must be. </div> </div> </div>Not at battle group scale. I doubt you'll ever see just a battle group of wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T19:14:04-07:00","id":276907,"title":"","content":"Ooh. Many thanks for the answers! ^__^ Very much looking forward to see the write-up on wolves. Also to what this suggests for some other critters. And, kinda relevant to the thread, ways this suggests shapeshifting can grant more tactically interesting options to a Lunar than prior editions.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in your latter answer in particular. From what I saw on the quotes wiki (and, er, quoted below in the spoiler block), I would have thought it likely a wolf pack might get abstracted into a battle group, if its individual members weren't sufficiently important/distinct as individuals. Would you have the freedom (and interest) to elaborate? I remembered from one of the playtest summaries Eric posted that a pack of hounds was made into a battle group. Might that have been in part because there was so much going on in that fight, such that a pack of (say) five hounds might have been individual actors if they were the only critters menacing the Circle?<br /> <br /> Spoilering what I typed up before spotting Vance's answers (got some quotes that might be relevant reading), for space reasons.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276856#post276856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would wager the point of a battle group is to easily represent a larger number of combatants than is feasible to run as individuals, combining that with notions of how groups of people fight together and react to fighting together.<br /> <br /> If an ST runs a mob of 20 angry peasants as a battle group, simply being a battle group shouldn't necessarily provide those 20 peasants or the Exalted they're fighting a super huge advantage or disadvantage over fighting 20 peasants as individuals. The point is to make it OOC easier to run such a combat (and end it in ways other than killing every discrete living thing inside the battle group) by having only one &quot;unit&quot; to interact with (as opposed to 20), with its own internal rules like &quot;for every X damage taken, suffer Y stat degradation and Z morale effect.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Simplification is indeed part of the reason, though story significance is another component. Some random wolf pack may become a battle group, meanwhile the Solar who was literally raised by wolves might find the members of his family important enough to be treated as individuals. It's possible there have been system revisions, but talk we got a while ago suggests there can be a difference in the difficulty of those fights, even if the actual number of wolves involved is the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, assuming we're fishing our ninjas out of clone tanks, a battle group of 100 ninjas is going to be stronger in an absolute sense than a single ninja, insofar as that it has bonuses the single guy doesn't. On the other hand, when you engage the single ninja, the system is going to process your conflict as a high-energy cinematic battle between two actors worth paying attention to; whereas when you engage the 100 ninja katamari, it's going to interpret that as you laying waste to a bunch of them with every attack, Bruce Lee style; so the one guy is going to seem tougher. If that one ninja is the ninja that killed your brother, then he's never going to get rolled into the katamari because he's story-significant; if he's one of the three ninjas that killed your brother, all three of them are going to always be rendered individually (and in this sense may be more dangerous than the ninja katamari simply because the nature of the system favors gang-up tactics over single big attacks in many situations). This isn't considered a problem, because a battle against the three ninjas that killed your brother should be more dramatic and memorable than chopping your way through the break room at 1-800-Rent-A-Ninja.</div> </div> </div> </div>They sound like they're trying to build in factors here that we've not fully seen to avoid perverse incentives. One of the factors we have is quoted below (which also answers part of my unexpressed-but-kinda-underlying question about what level of distance or being &quot;unattached&quot; from one another would cover battle grouping characters who aren't distinct enough to be individuals).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: (Mizu005)</b><br /> Hmm, I'm going to go out on a limb and assume that you are free to divide a group into separate blobs instead of one blob as it suits you.<br /> <br /> <b>A: (Holden)</b><br /> You're not, actually. You're only allowed to split a group if it's geographically divided WAY the fuck apart-- like, at opposite ends of a valley doing a pincer maneuver. Otherwise, you keep stacking on until you hit the maximum size for a BG, and only then start a new one.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T20:16:17-07:00","id":276939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276907#post276907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in your latter answer in particular. From what I saw on the quotes wiki (and, er, quoted below in the spoiler block), I would have thought it likely a wolf pack might get abstracted into a battle group, if its individual members weren't sufficiently important/distinct as individuals. Would you have the freedom (and interest) to elaborate? I remembered from one of the playtest summaries Eric posted that a pack of hounds was made into a battle group. Might that have been in part because there was so much going on in that fight, such that a pack of (say) five hounds might have been individual actors if they were the only critters menacing the Circle?</div> </div> </div> </div>In stories/movies/whatever, whenever you have a conflict with wolves, velociraptors, anything that falls into that kind of pack hunter archetype, it tends to emphasize the threat of a small number of coordinated, deadly predators. Think Jurassic Park. On the other hand, if the wolves are only one actor in a larger fight and not really the primary focus, you could just collapse them all into a battle group. I don't really expect the latter situation to happen much, if ever, but there's no reason it couldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T20:23:45-07:00","id":276946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276939#post276939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In stories/movies/whatever, whenever you have a conflict with wolves, velociraptors, anything that falls into that kind of pack hunter archetype, it tends to emphasize the threat of a small number of coordinated, deadly predators. Think Jurassic Park. On the other hand, if the wolves are only one actor in a larger fight and not really the primary focus, you could just collapse them all into a battle group. I don't really expect the latter situation to happen much, if ever, but there's no reason it couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if I am a wild-man Solar, raised with wolves and fighting alongside them?<br /> <br /> (speaking personally, I'd like my wolves to be differenciated, I think, rather than blended into a single unit that gets mowed down with every successful hit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T20:25:50-07:00","id":276947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276946#post276946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I am a wild-man Solar, raised with wolves and fighting alongside them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then your enemies are gonna come down with a bad case of having their throats ripped out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T20:27:21-07:00","id":276950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276947#post276947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then your enemies are gonna come down with a bad case of having their throats ripped out.</div> </div> </div> </div>*happiness sounds*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T20:28:50-07:00","id":276951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276946#post276946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I am a wild-man Solar, raised with wolves and fighting alongside them?<br /> <br /> (speaking personally, I'd like my wolves to be differenciated, I think, rather than blended into a single unit that gets mowed down with every successful hit)</div> </div> </div> </div>A small number would work as Vance described and means running them as individual combatants, not using a battle group.<br /> <br /> A wild man Solar running by his pack of wolves is the same notion as a Solar archer/houndmaster shooting a foe with a pack of hound-Familiars in melee. In neither case do the dogs use the rules of a battle group unless, I suppose, <i>you just have so many of them that it's totally unwieldy not to</i>. That's a sweet spot for every group to find but I would DOUBT that anything above 10 dogs or so is going to be feasible to run as individual animals with individual initiative scores etc. That kind of volume will slow any group down. If the pacing suffers because you have 20 dog-familairs, you should probably just use a battle group: story-significance or no it just isn't worth slowing the game down that much to avoid the additional level of abstraction that a battle group represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T20:36:42-07:00","id":276954,"title":"","content":"I am reminded of <i>the Mo\u00efra</i>, a French fantasy book trilogy.<br /> <br /> In it, the heroine has a strange link with a she-wolf that goes around gathering other wolves into a huge wolf army that eventually arrives as the Third Act Cavalry of one epic battle.<br /> <br /> I imagine <i>those</i> wolves would be a battle group, because there's hundreds of them.<br /> <br /> And they kick much ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T04:56:23-07:00","id":277103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276418#post276418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, remember when Lunars had shapeshifting powers?<br /> <br /> By all means, let's get rid of the extraneous crap that doesn't really make sense with &quot;zoanthropic shapeshifting demigod&quot;. But when people start arguing that a Lunar can't become a pack of wolves despite the power to become a swarm of bees, I'm going to get pissy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pack of wolves is pushing it a bit, Dragon Ball or Naruto multiform is jumping right over the edge.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And don't pretend you were being specific about shapeshifting when you brought out the kludgeon on &quot;if you take things Lunars never had away from them, they'll have nothing at all!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T05:57:26-07:00","id":277129,"title":"","content":"I'll just chime in to say that I'm a fan of swarm-forms. This is not without a certain level of bias; Computational Intelligence is my area of focus and swarm intelligence is a favorite optimization paradigm. It's just fun and fascinating. And letting Lunars parallelize themselves sounds like a fun and cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T07:13:37-07:00","id":277194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=276856#post276856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>The existence of battle groups is not merely an abstraction - we've actually already been told such, IIRC. It's a deliberate means of enabling some of the mythic, pulp, and wuxia elements that go into Exalted to be properly invoked - whether it's Conan taking on twenty assassins entering his chamber in the dead of night, Samson taking on thousands of Philistines by himself, or Sky fighting all those swordsmen in <i>Hero</i>. <br /> <br /> With the devs and writers pressing firmly to the &quot;no one will be passively invulnerable&quot; line for Ex3, representing these kinds of fights <i>without</i> battle-groups means it's likely even Sun Wukong will get his shit wrecked in a fight with enough participants in the enemy side. And no one wants that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T07:23:27-07:00","id":277209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275424#post275424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I feel that it's difficult to use the Monkey King as a reference point for Lunars, because so many of his own powers are a matter of his Taoist instruction and alchemical transformation rather than his own body... which is itself more weird magic stuff than animalistic person, considering that he was born from a stone).</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like the same kind of thinking that invalidates Sherlock Holmes or Batman as Solar inspirations, simply because they aren't framed as being touched by the divine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T08:18:56-07:00","id":277235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=277103#post277103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pack of wolves is pushing it a bit, Dragon Ball or Naruto multiform is jumping right over the edge.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And don't pretend you were being specific about shapeshifting when you brought out the kludgeon on &quot;if you take things Lunars never had away from them, they'll have nothing at all!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also a bit redundant to be able to bark out bees and also become a swarm of them. I'd rather stick with the production of a swarm than with becoming one, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T09:18:37-07:00","id":277283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=277235#post277235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also a bit redundant to be able to bark out bees and also become a swarm of them. I'd rather stick with the production of a swarm than with becoming one, myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why. They have different applications. One gives you a swarm minion; the other lets you be the swarm. The swarm minion has its own action(s), but is not you and thus lacks your skills and magic. The swarm you become has your stats, powers, magics, and understanding of situations, and lets you personally benefit from the advantages of being a swarm (such as getting out of tight spaces, flowing around things, and being hard to hurt on any macroscopic scale).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T10:20:04-07:00","id":277341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=277194#post277194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the devs and writers pressing firmly to the &quot;no one will be passively invulnerable&quot; line for Ex3, representing these kinds of fights <i>without</i> battle-groups means it's likely even Sun Wukong will get his shit wrecked in a fight with enough participants in the enemy side. And no one wants that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh why exactly would no one want that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T11:04:42-07:00","id":277384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=277341#post277341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh why exactly would no one want that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the sentence directly above the one you quoted. Myth, pulp, wuxia, and the like are <i>brimming</i> with fights between heroes and armies, and if you remove the ability to tell those kinds of stories, you're doing a massive disservice to Exalted.<br /> <br /> EDIT: By &quot;enough participants,&quot; I mean like ten, far less impressive than the twenty or so rogues Conan survived, or the <i>hundred thousand</i> Sun Wukong defeated in a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-10-2014, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T11:39:43-07:00","id":277419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=277283#post277283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why. They have different applications. One gives you a swarm minion; the other lets you be the swarm. The swarm minion has its own action(s), but is not you and thus lacks your skills and magic. The swarm you become has your stats, powers, magics, and understanding of situations, and lets you personally benefit from the advantages of being a swarm (such as getting out of tight spaces, flowing around things, and being hard to hurt on any macroscopic scale).</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what else allows you to fit into tight spaces? Just turning into a small shape, as a single being. You could also just hide in the swarm that you conjured up with this method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:53:02-07:00","id":277510,"title":"","content":"Yes, but you are still not the swarm, so you're not everywhere that it is. And you're one of the things in it, which means you can be targetted specifically. There are a number of things you can do as a swarm that you can't as a single tiny thing. Parallelization is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T13:03:52-07:00","id":277514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=277103#post277103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't pretend you were being specific about shapeshifting when you brought out the kludgeon on &quot;if you take things Lunars never had away from them, they'll have nothing at all!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I won't pretend. Because I wouldn't have to pretend, given that's exactly what I was talking about. (Certainly, this thread was never <i>about </i>any other kind of Lunar ability.)<br /> <br /> Also, Lunars already had Ant and Starfish Trick for self-cloning shenanigans. Granted, it sucked ass compared to certain Adjorani Charms, but it was there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T13:10:11-07:00","id":277517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=277514#post277514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Lunars already had Ant and Starfish Trick for self-cloning shenanigans. Granted, it sucked ass compared to certain Adjorani Charms, but it was there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question is more &quot;should it have been?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T14:51:52-07:00","id":277574,"title":"","content":"I could see Lunars splitting into copies <i>momentarily</i>, as a sort of Cascade of Biting Terror or Forest of Shadow Images thing. But I wouldn't handle them as distinct beings, because that goes too much down the road of making Lunars the &quot;Craft (Genesis) Exalted&quot;, and I think they went too far in that direction in 2e, despite ironically being very bad at Craft (Genesis).<br /> <br /> That said, in 3e terms I'll accept any sufficiently interesting, compelling vision of Lunars. It's not what I'd do, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 10-10-2014, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T08:29:16-07:00","id":278153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming#post273974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the appropriate upper limits on Lunar's giant-ness, massive swarm-ness, and Kage Bunshin-ness?</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion on giant Lunars.<br /> <br /> Giant Lunars are (currently) problematic because either they stay in these forms most of the time and become behemoths in all but name or they use the form tactically and ignore the logistical problems of using behemoths but we're left to assume anything they went kaiju on was destroyed with no witnesses or survivors.... take our word for it they're hardcore!<br /> <br /> I'd sooner see Heart Theft of the Behemoth return than Emperor Ox Expansion that way the biggest Lunar is a matter of achievement rather than essence rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T09:49:28-07:00","id":278189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=277574#post277574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see Lunars splitting into copies <i>momentarily</i>, as a sort of Cascade of Biting Terror or Forest of Shadow Images thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would definitely be one way to limit &quot;I cover the land in BEES&quot;, which really ought to be the scale of Sorcery. Like, maybe you could envelop and attack an entire town at once as a swarm of bees, but the swarm vanishes at the end of the attack or round and you need to pay in full to do it over again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=278153#post278153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion on giant Lunars.<br /> <br /> Giant Lunars are (currently) problematic because either they stay in these forms most of the time and become behemoths in all but name or they use the form tactically and ignore the logistical problems of using behemoths but we're left to assume anything they went kaiju on was destroyed with no witnesses or survivors.... take our word for it they're hardcore!<br /> <br /> I'd sooner see Heart Theft of the Behemoth return than Emperor Ox Expansion that way the biggest Lunar is a matter of achievement rather than essence rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Essence rating is itself a matter of achievement, but I agree with the spirit of the rest of your points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T14:27:24-07:00","id":278347,"title":"","content":"From a strictly out of character perspective high-essence tends to be assigned to NPCs by going &quot;this character is an elder&quot; and working backwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T18:06:42-07:00","id":278506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=278153#post278153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion on giant Lunars.<br /> <br /> Giant Lunars are (currently) problematic because either they stay in these forms most of the time and become behemoths in all but name or they use the form tactically and ignore the logistical problems of using behemoths but we're left to assume anything they went kaiju on was destroyed with no witnesses or survivors.... take our word for it they're hardcore!<br /> <br /> I'd sooner see Heart Theft of the Behemoth return than Emperor Ox Expansion that way the biggest Lunar is a matter of achievement rather than essence rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with huge size is apparently that they put all of the rules for dealing with it in MoEP: Abyssals, in the &quot;Necrotech&quot; section to be exact, and didn't bother to tell people that they might also apply to huge things that weren't reanimated monsters. What's more, it didn't really tell you how big something was very clearly. You had to work back from equivalent size mutations and descriptions of reanimated horrors to get a ballpark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:13:47-07:00","id":954386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=275021#post275021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect to see Lunars becoming their own battle groups even if they do have an &quot;I'm hella bees&quot; prana. Battle groups are a useful mechanical shorthand for depicting groups of combatants, but when every member of that group is just a separate body of the same entity, a lot of the mechanics are going to get confused and that particular lens becomes useless. I would expect a swarm transformation to have rules based on representing a person who has dissolved into a swarm of things, or combined it with some kind of kaiju transformation to become a giant death-swarm, rather than catch on to a system hook that really doesn't support them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Robert. Hey Robert. Roooooobert.<br /> <br /> <i>Miracles of the Solar Exalted.</i> &quot;Faster Than Self Technique.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T00:19:06-07:00","id":954869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/273974-limits-on-lunar-size-and-swarming?p=954386#post954386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robert. Hey Robert. Roooooobert.<br /> <br /> <i>Miracles of the Solar Exalted.</i> &amp;quot;Faster Than Self Technique.&amp;quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/to